---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = "Mortgage Consultation Miami | Talk Through Loan Options";
const description = "Schedule or request a Miami mortgage consultation to compare FHA, conventional, VA, jumbo, condo, self-employed, DSCR, refinance, and investor options.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
<main id="main"><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Consultation page</p><h1>Mortgage Consultation Miami</h1><p>Talk through the mortgage scenario before applying, making an offer, or choosing between loan programs.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Scenario Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Calculate Payment</a></div><div class="trust-row"><span class="trust-pill">Matthew Gromadzki</span><span class="trust-pill">NMLS #2560919</span><span class="trust-pill">Miami-Dade focused</span></div></div><form class="lead-form"><h2>Mortgage Consultation Miami Form</h2><p>Share the basics so the right mortgage path can be reviewed.</p><label>Mortgage goal<select><option>Select one</option><option>Purchase</option><option>Refinance</option><option>Cash-out refinance</option><option>Condo review</option><option>Investor / DSCR</option><option>Self-employed borrower</option></select></label><div class="form-row"><label>Property city<input placeholder="Miami, Brickell, Doral..."></label><label>Property type<select><option>Select one</option><option>Single-family</option><option>Condo</option><option>Townhome</option><option>Multi-unit</option><option>Investment property</option></select></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Price or value<input placeholder="$650,000"></label><label>Down payment / equity<input placeholder="10%, 20%, $100k..."></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Credit range<select><option>Select range</option><option>760+</option><option>720-759</option><option>680-719</option><option>640-679</option><option>600-639</option></select></label><label>Income type<select><option>Select type</option><option>W-2</option><option>Self-employed</option><option>1099</option><option>Investor / rental</option><option>Foreign national</option></select></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Name<input></label><label>Phone<input></label></div><label>Email<input type="email"></label><label>Notes<textarea rows="4" placeholder="Condo building, deadline, loan questions..."></textarea></label><button class="btn btn-primary full" type="button">Send Scenario</button></form></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><article class="prose"><p>Mortgage Consultation Miami is designed for Miami-Dade borrowers who want a cleaner answer before they apply, submit an offer, lock a rate, or compare lenders. The goal is to turn a vague mortgage question into a structured scenario with property type, price, down payment, credit range, income documentation, city, and timeline.</p><p>Some borrowers need a quote. Others need a broader conversation about loan options, documentation, property type, timing, and strategy. This page is designed to capture consultation-intent traffic without forcing every visitor into a full application path.</p><p>The goal is to give you enough detail to trust the process, then point you to a quote, preapproval, the calculator, or the right guide for your situation.</p><h2>Who should use this mortgage review path</h2><p>Use this page when the borrower has a specific mortgage question but is not ready for a full application. It is especially useful for borrowers comparing programs, buying a condo, changing down payment assumptions, or trying to understand how payment and cash to close will look in Miami-Dade.</p><p>For mortgage consultation miami, a short form is not enough unless the right questions are asked. The page should collect the property city, property type, loan purpose, estimated price or value, down payment or equity, credit range, income type, occupancy, and timing.</p><p>The review should not promise approval or a rate. It should identify which loan programs are worth comparing and what documents or property details are needed before a reliable quote can be issued.</p><h2>What should be reviewed before quoting</h2><p>A consultation should clarify the borrower goal, timeline, property type, budget, credit range, income type, down payment/equity, and whether there are any known challenges.</p><p>For Miami condos, the review should include HOA dues, master insurance, project status, reserves, litigation, special assessments, rental restrictions, and whether the loan program fits the building. For jumbo or self-employed files, reserves and documentation can be just as important as the rate.</p><p>The best lead experience is a guided scenario review: borrowers answer only the questions needed for their situation, then receive a next-step recommendation instead of a generic sales pitch.</p><h2>Documents and details that improve accuracy</h2><p>Prepare the basic scenario, questions, current documents if available, and any deadlines. The consultation can then point to preapproval, quote, calculator, or a specific loan page.</p><p>A buyer does not need to upload everything just to start, but the more accurate the scenario, the more useful the response. Estimated taxes, HOA dues, insurance assumptions, credit score range, and target closing date are especially important in Miami-Dade.</p><p>If the borrower is already under contract, the property address, contract price, association dues, deadline dates, and building information should be collected immediately.</p></article><aside><div class="content-card"><h2>Useful related paths</h2><ul><li><a href="about.html">About Matthew Gromadzki</a></li><li><a href="licenses-and-disclosures.html">Licenses and Disclosures</a></li><li><a href="start.html">Request a Mortgage Quote</a></li><li><a href="get-preapproved-miami.html">Get Preapproved in Miami</a></li><li><a href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Florida Mortgage Calculator</a></li><li><a href="miami-mortgage-guides.html">Miami Mortgage Guides</a></li><li><a href="mortgage-broker-miami.html">Mortgage Broker Miami</a></li></ul></div></aside></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fast next step</p><h2>Send the scenario before you make the mortgage decision.</h2><p>Use the quote or preapproval path to compare payment, cash to close, property review, and documentation needs.</p></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="tel:+13059884806">Call (305) 988-4806</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p><h2>Mortgage Consultation Miami FAQ</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is mortgage consultation miami the same as a loan application?</summary><p>No. A scenario review or checklist is an early planning step. A full application, documentation, credit review, underwriting, appraisal, title, insurance, and property review may still be required.</p></details><details><summary>Can this page guarantee approval or a specific interest rate?</summary><p>No. Loan approval, rate, terms, closing costs, and program availability depend on lender guidelines, documentation, underwriting, property review, market conditions, and timing.</p></details><details><summary>Should I use the calculator before requesting a quote?</summary><p>Yes. A calculator can help estimate payment, but a quote should also review taxes, homeowners insurance, flood or wind coverage, HOA dues, mortgage insurance, closing costs, and cash to close.</p></details><details><summary>What is the fastest next step?</summary><p>Submit a mortgage scenario with property city, purpose, price or value, down payment or equity, credit range, income type, and timeline. If you are shopping soon, request preapproval before making an offer.</p></details></div></div></section></main>
</BaseLayout>
